/// The life of one queued message.
///
/// SENT and DELIVERED are deliberately different states. SENT means the provider accepted
/// it; DELIVERED means the network said it arrived. On Nigerian networks the gap between
/// those two is where DND blocking lives - a message charged for, accepted, and never
/// delivered - so collapsing them would hide exactly the failure a school needs to see.
